          "guid": "mrwoi9n7mkye3d4a",
          "message": {
            "text": "Bumped CHANNEL_VERSION/EXPECTED_CHANNEL_VERSION 18 → 19 even though no MCP tool or HTTP endpoint changed: an already-running v18 channel server will not read `HOTSHEET_DRIVE_SPAWNED` or write the `drive` registry field, so the bogus warning would persist for that connection until reconnect. The version-mismatch nudge (\"reconnect via /mcp\") is the existing mechanism that gets users onto server code that understands the marker.\n",
            "markdown": "Bumped CHANNEL_VERSION/EXPECTED_CHANNEL_VERSION 18 → 19 even though no MCP tool or HTTP endpoint changed: an already-running v18 channel server will not read `HOTSHEET_DRIVE_SPAWNED` or write the `drive` registry field, so the bogus warning would persist for that connection until reconnect. The version-mismatch nudge (\"reconnect via /mcp\") is the existing mechanism that gets users onto server code that understands the marker.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/channel-config.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 248,
                  "endLine": 254,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": " *  registry, so the main server will continue to see only the v8\n *  entry via the legacy `channel-port` file — `/mcp` reconnect\n *  respawns at v9 and populates the registry.\n *  Users who have the channel registered will see a \"reconnect via `/mcp`\"\n *  prompt when the main server boots with the newer version. */\n// HS-9112 — bumped 16 → 17 in lockstep with `CHANNEL_VERSION` (src/channel.ts)\n// for the new `hotsheet_propose_partition` MCP tool. A running v16 channel prompts"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
